  26:     3. Build closed outlines as 1-pixel-thick rectilinear loops (irregular polygons with 8-14 corners, bbox 6x6 to 13x11). Place non-overlapping on the grid with min manhattan gap >= 3.
  27:     4. Optionally build 1 open outline as a 1-pixel-thick rectilinear path (no enclosed region).
  28:     5. For each closed outline, flood-fill its enclosed interior to determine the fill region.
  29:     6. For each enclosed region, pick a majority marker color (distinct from outline colors and bg). Place 2-6 marker pixels of that color inside the region, plus 1-2 minority-color markers (fewer count than majority). Record the fill color = majority color.
  30:     7. The output is: outlines + filled interiors. The input is: outlines + marker pixels inside regions (unfilled interior is bg) + 0-14 stray marker pixels scattered on bg cells outside all outlines.
